{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570507967,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bca9aa002bqeqzEoizdoPLY","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","messageID":"msg_1d4bc9308001olPqi2dkSwdZaX","type":"tool","id":"call_c93602d207cd48da8a33c930","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - embed-text-4 (richer command embedding text)\ndescription: Measures what richer command embedding text buys the six no-recommendation commands on a scratch copy of the advisor database and command metadata, against the built state after phases 014 and 015.\ntrigger_phrases: []\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n# Deep Research Strategy - embed-text-4\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nLane label `embed-text-4`: segment four, rank 10 and open question 5 of segment three. Measure what richer command embedding text buys the six no-recommendation commands. The measurement runs on a scratch copy of the advisor database and a scratch set of intent signals; no tracked file changes.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nSegment four embed-text lane. Segment three rank 10 proposes giving the six no-recommendation commands evidence through command intent signals, with `/create:skill-parent` also needing a scorer row. Segment three open question 5 asks whether richer intent text in the skill or command vectors moves holdout rows. Rank 16 (enriching skill intent signals and re-embedding the skill graph) is already declined; this lane measures the command side only.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] KQ1: What are the before numbers at HEAD after phases 014 and 015, using the committed capture in `--real-embedding` mode against a scratch copy of the database: plain tune recall, false offers of 35, the holdout count, and the three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82?\n- [ ] KQ2: When the six no-recommendation commands get richer intent signals in scratch copies of their owning metadata and their command vectors are re-embedded with the live embedder, what changes in the same capture: tune recall, false offers of 35, holdout count, and the three doctor-family floor rows?\n- [ ] KQ3: Does the measured gain justify a build, with the exact files and the measured gain, or a decline, with the number; and which of the six cannot benefit until it has a scorer row?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending anything ranked, built, declined or waiting in segments one, two and three, including segment three rank 16 (skill intent signals) and rank 8 (quality-control aliases).\n- Changing any tracked file: the database, command metadata, bridge projection, scorer, config and corpus stay read-only.\n- Running a model session, an arena or the full suite; writing outside the lineage directory.\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text. Holdout rows are counted only through the committed capture.\n- Building the change itself; this lane reports whether to build it and with what numbers.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below, with every key question answered or explicitly carried forward.\n- Eight iterations at most; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\n- Stop early when a further iteration would add no new measurement, and say which measurement is missing.\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- Segment three rank 10: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md` lines 75 and 95.\n- Segment three open question 5: same file, line 209.\n- The six no-recommendation commands and their causes: same file, lines 106-107: five have a scorer row and return nothing (`/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update`, `/speckit:search`), and `/create:skill-parent` has no scorer row.\n- The three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82: `mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01`, `sv-03` (same file, line 37).\n- The live embedder: Ollama at `127.0.0.1:11434`, model `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, 768 dimensions, records stored as `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` in `vec_cmd_768`.\n- The committed capture: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (`--real-embedding`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` selects the database directory).\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts`, `lib/command-attach.ts`, `scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json`.\n- Reuse candidates: the committed capture script and its real-embedding preflight; the runtime's command vector table and content-hash convention.\n- Constraints: no tracked file writes; no holdout text; scratch DB and scratch metadata only.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 15 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n- Question injection surface: `research/inbox.jsonl`\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T11:47:27Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - embed-text-4 (richer command embedding text)\\ndescription: Measures what richer command embedding text buys the six no-recommendation commands on a scratch copy of the advisor database and command metadata, against the built state after phases 014 and 015.\\ntrigger_phrases: []\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n# Deep Research Strategy - embed-text-4\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\nLane label `embed-text-4`: segment four, rank 10 and open question 5 of segment three. Measure what richer command embedding text buys the six no-recommendation commands. The measurement runs on a scratch copy of the advisor database and a scratch set of intent signals; no tracked file changes.\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nSegment four embed-text lane. Segment three rank 10 proposes giving the six no-recommendation commands evidence through command intent signals, with `/create:skill-parent` also needing a scorer row. Segment three open question 5 asks whether richer intent text in the skill or command vectors moves holdout rows. Rank 16 (enriching skill intent signals and re-embedding the skill graph) is already declined; this lane measures the command side only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] KQ1: What are the before numbers at HEAD after phases 014 and 015, using the committed capture in `--real-embedding` mode against a scratch copy of the database: plain tune recall, false offers of 35, the holdout count, and the three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82?\\n- [ ] KQ2: When the six no-recommendation commands get richer intent signals in scratch copies of their owning metadata and their command vectors are re-embedded with the live embedder, what changes in the same capture: tune recall, false offers of 35, holdout count, and the three doctor-family floor rows?\\n- [ ] KQ3: Does the measured gain justify a build, with the exact files and the measured gain, or a decline, with the number; and which of the six cannot benefit until it has a scorer row?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending anything ranked, built, declined or waiting in segments one, two and three, including segment three rank 16 (skill intent signals) and rank 8 (quality-control aliases).\\n- Changing any tracked file: the database, command metadata, bridge projection, scorer, config and corpus stay read-only.\\n- Running a model session, an arena or the full suite; writing outside the lineage directory.\\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text. Holdout rows are counted only through the committed capture.\\n- Building the change itself; this lane reports whether to build it and with what numbers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below, with every key question answered or explicitly carried forward.\\n- Eight iterations at most; a thin iteration is recorded with status `timeout` or `stuck`, not skipped.\\n- Stop early when a further iteration would add no new measurement, and say which measurement is missing.\\n- Stop early only for unrecoverable state corruption or a missing control file.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n[Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n- Segment three rank 10: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md` lines 75 and 95.\\n- Segment three open question 5: same file, line 209.\\n- The six no-recommendation commands and their causes: same file, lines 106-107: five have a scorer row and return nothing (`/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update`, `/speckit:search`), and `/create:skill-parent` has no scorer row.\\n- The three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82: `mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01`, `sv-03` (same file, line 37).\\n- The live embedder: Ollama at `127.0.0.1:11434`, model `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, 768 dimensions, records stored as `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` in `vec_cmd_768`.\\n- The committed capture: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (`--real-embedding`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` selects the database directory).\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts`, `lib/command-attach.ts`, `scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json`.\\n- Reuse candidates: the committed capture script and its real-embedding preflight; the runtime's command vector table and content-hash convention.\\n- Constraints: no tracked file writes; no holdout text; scratch DB and scratch metadata only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 15 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true (default)\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\\n- Question injection surface: `research/inbox.jsonl`\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T11:47:27Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570496426,"end":1794570507967}}}}
