{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794570591774,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","part":{"id":"prt_1d4be1e1e0019skAdd7ZjTQ3Eq","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","messageID":"msg_1d4be17bc001DuT5eShPLNSB6X","type":"step-start","snapshot":"7980fabe3c50f7c5797142b834bf884b0ed9159e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570607045,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4be1f8a001izyrdM6atCW5zh","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","messageID":"msg_1d4be17bc001DuT5eShPLNSB6X","type":"tool","id":"call_504e40bcaf254abd810d21d7","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: Baseline capture on a scratch copy of the advisor database\n\n## Focus\n\nKQ1: measure the before numbers at HEAD after phases 014 and 015 with the committed capture in `--real-embedding` mode against a scratch copy of the advisor database. The lane needs this baseline before any intent signal or vector changes so the after numbers differ only by the enrichment.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the lane inputs: `goals.md`, segment three sections 3 and 4, the phase 014 and 015 summaries, the committed capture script, the skill-graph vector schema and the command-bridge deriver.\n2. Took a consistent snapshot of the live advisor database with `sqlite3 ... \".backup '<lineage>/scratch/db-before/skill-graph.sqlite'\"`, which gave 14 skill nodes, 46 command vectors and the active embedder `nomic-embed-text-v1.5`.\n3. Ran the committed capture in its real-embedding mode with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` pointing at that snapshot:\n   `env SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR=\"$PWD/<lineage>/scratch/db-before\" node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding`\n   It exited 0 in 12.5 s and wrote `scratch/before-capture.json`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. At HEAD `087888ec4a` the real-embedding capture reads typed recall 24 of 44, plain tune top-1 13 of 45, plain tune combined reach 28 of 45 (13 own plus 15 attached), plain holdout top-1 3 of 44, false offers 0 of 35 and `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:618-658]\n2. The three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82 offer no command: `mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01` and `sv-03` all top `system-skilled-doctor` with `offered: false`, `top1: false` and `top3: false`. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json]\n3. Each of the five scored no-recommendation commands has exactly one tune row and one holdout row, and every one is 0 at top-1 and 0 at top-3: `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search`. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl]\n4. `/create:skill-parent` has no TypeScript bridge: it is in the capture's `unreachable` list, its typed row tops `sk-doc`, and its plain row carries no command. No command-vector change can reach it until a scorer row exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json]\n5. The scratch-database lane is faithful and repeatable: the capture exits 0, the database snapshot holds the same 46 command vectors and the same active embedder as the live file, and its numbers equal the segment-three real capture (13 of 45 tune, 3 of 44 holdout, 0 of 35 false offers). [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md:39]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Running the capture against the live database in place: it would measure whatever the daemon wrote and would leave no before snapshot for the after run.\n- A plain file copy of the WAL-mode database: the `-wal` file may hold committed rows, so `.backup` was used for a consistent snapshot.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- None yet. The lane has a working baseline and a scratch copy that the enrichment run can reuse.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none. The six commands and the three floor rows are named by segment three, and the capture publishes only holdout counts.\n- Contradictory evidence: none. The baseline agrees with the segment-three real capture.\n- Missing dependencies: none. Ollama answers with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, and the scratch database holds the `vec_cmd_768` table.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md:60-116`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/implementation-summary.md:45-60`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:134-184,346-430,618-658`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:290-324,740-812,1484-1590`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:25-40,660-700`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.45\n- Questions addressed: KQ1\n- Questions answered: KQ1\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: `sqlite3 .backup` plus the capture's documented `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` override made the whole lane possible without touching a tracked file. The committed capture's real-embedding preflight also proved the embedder and the command-vector table before a single row was scored, so a silent cosine lane could not be mistaken for a scoring result.\n- What did not work and why: nothing failed. Reading the generated bridge projection rather than each metadata file was enough to see that `/create:skill-parent` has no TypeScript runtime, which explains its zero without a vector run.\n- What I would do differently: nothing for this iteration; the next run can reuse the same snapshot and change only the six command vectors.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nKQ2: compose richer intent signals for the six commands, write them only in the lineage scratch folder, re-embed the six command vectors in a second copy of the database, and rerun the same capture to compare tune recall, false offers of 35, the holdout count and the three doctor-family floor rows.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 1: Baseline capture on a scratch copy of the advisor database\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nKQ1: measure the before numbers at HEAD after phases 014 and 015 with the committed capture in `--real-embedding` mode against a scratch copy of the advisor database. The lane needs this baseline before any intent signal or vector changes so the after numbers differ only by the enrichment.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the lane inputs: `goals.md`, segment three sections 3 and 4, the phase 014 and 015 summaries, the committed capture script, the skill-graph vector schema and the command-bridge deriver.\\n2. Took a consistent snapshot of the live advisor database with `sqlite3 ... \\\".backup '<lineage>/scratch/db-before/skill-graph.sqlite'\\\"`, which gave 14 skill nodes, 46 command vectors and the active embedder `nomic-embed-text-v1.5`.\\n3. Ran the committed capture in its real-embedding mode with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` pointing at that snapshot:\\n   `env SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR=\\\"$PWD/<lineage>/scratch/db-before\\\" node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding`\\n   It exited 0 in 12.5 s and wrote `scratch/before-capture.json`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. At HEAD `087888ec4a` the real-embedding capture reads typed recall 24 of 44, plain tune top-1 13 of 45, plain tune combined reach 28 of 45 (13 own plus 15 attached), plain holdout top-1 3 of 44, false offers 0 of 35 and `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:618-658]\\n2. The three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82 offer no command: `mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01` and `sv-03` all top `system-skilled-doctor` with `offered: false`, `top1: false` and `top3: false`. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json]\\n3. Each of the five scored no-recommendation commands has exactly one tune row and one holdout row, and every one is 0 at top-1 and 0 at top-3: `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search`. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl]\\n4. `/create:skill-parent` has no TypeScript bridge: it is in the capture's `unreachable` list, its typed row tops `sk-doc`, and its plain row carries no command. No command-vector change can reach it until a scorer row exists. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json]\\n5. The scratch-database lane is faithful and repeatable: the capture exits 0, the database snapshot holds the same 46 command vectors and the same active embedder as the live file, and its numbers equal the segment-three real capture (13 of 45 tune, 3 of 44 holdout, 0 of 35 false offers). [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md:39]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Running the capture against the live database in place: it would measure whatever the daemon wrote and would leave no before snapshot for the after run.\\n- A plain file copy of the WAL-mode database: the `-wal` file may hold committed rows, so `.backup` was used for a consistent snapshot.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- None yet. The lane has a working baseline and a scratch copy that the enrichment run can reuse.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: none. The six commands and the three floor rows are named by segment three, and the capture publishes only holdout counts.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none. The baseline agrees with the segment-three real capture.\\n- Missing dependencies: none. Ollama answers with `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, and the scratch database holds the `vec_cmd_768` table.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md:60-116`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/implementation-summary.md:45-60`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:134-184,346-430,618-658`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:290-324,740-812,1484-1590`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:25-40,660-700`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/scratch/before-capture.json`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.45\\n- Questions addressed: KQ1\\n- Questions answered: KQ1\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: `sqlite3 .backup` plus the capture's documented `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR` override made the whole lane possible without touching a tracked file. The committed capture's real-embedding preflight also proved the embedder and the command-vector table before a single row was scored, so a silent cosine lane could not be mistaken for a scoring result.\\n- What did not work and why: nothing failed. Reading the generated bridge projection rather than each metadata file was enough to see that `/create:skill-parent` has no TypeScript runtime, which explains its zero without a vector run.\\n- What I would do differently: nothing for this iteration; the next run can reuse the same snapshot and change only the six command vectors.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nKQ2: compose richer intent signals for the six commands, write them only in the lineage scratch folder, re-embed the six command vectors in a second copy of the database, and rerun the same capture to compare tune recall, false offers of 35, the holdout count and the three doctor-family floor rows.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570592138,"end":1794570607045}}}}
