{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794571274229,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","part":{"id":"prt_1d4c887f5001GPJ6F2EyrjtUiW","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","messageID":"msg_1d4c87c960014R2oR8QiNeqUqh","type":"step-start","snapshot":"8cff73de69a5b7a1d6440d8a84fcfc9aa12e6fe8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571300656,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c898eb002OJWlbqhwfYoo6O","sessionID":"ses_e2b4abd5affeHy554lSqReHMR4","messageID":"msg_1d4c87c960014R2oR8QiNeqUqh","type":"tool","id":"call_d00e370f587a4be09129fa7c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: \"Embed text lane, segment four: what richer command embedding text buys\"\ndescription: \"Measured answer for segment-three rank 10 and open question 5: richer intent signals and re-embedded command vectors move five no-recommendation commands on tune and two on holdout, with every floor held.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"command embedding text research\"\n  - \"six no-recommendation commands\"\n  - \"segment four embed text lane\"\n---\n\n# Embed Text Lane: What Richer Command Embedding Text Buys\n\nLane `embed-text-4` of research segment four, measured on the built state after phases 014 and 015 at HEAD `087888ec4a`. Executor: `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` through `cli-opencode`. Three iterations, convergence threshold 0.05, stop reason `all_questions_answered`.\n\n## 1. What Was Measured\n\nSegment three rank 10 proposed giving the six no-recommendation commands evidence through command intent signals, with `/create:skill-parent` also needing a scorer row. Segment three open question 5 asked whether richer intent text in the command vectors moves holdout rows. This lane isolated the command-vector half:\n\n1. Took a consistent `.backup` snapshot of the live advisor database.\n2. Added 4 to 5 intent signals per command in scratch copies of the owning metadata (the two real `command-metadata.json` files plus a command-metadata-shaped sidecar for the four doctor routes, whose tracked home is `_routes.yaml`).\n3. Re-embedded only the five commands that own a stored vector, using the live embedder (`nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, `search_document: ` prefix).\n4. Ran the committed capture in `--real-embedding` mode against the scratch database and compared it with the same capture against the untouched snapshot.\n\nThe tracked metadata, database, bridge projection and corpus were never modified. Every write is inside `research/lineages/embed-text-4/`.\n\n## 2. Baseline at HEAD `087888ec4a`\n\n| Measure | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Typed recall at 1 | 24 of 44 |\n| Plain tune top-1 | 13 of 45 |\n| Plain tune combined reach (own + attached) | 28 of 45 |\n| Plain holdout top-1 | 3 of 44 |\n| False offers | 0 of 35 |\n| `needs_mode_floor` | 1 of 35 |\n\nThe three doctor-family floor rows that pass the gate at 0.82 (`mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01`, `sv-03`) all topped `system-skilled-doctor` and carried no command. Each of the five scored no-recommendation commands had one tune row and one holdout row at zero top-1 and zero top-3. `/create:skill-parent` was in the capture's `unreachable` list.\n\nEvidence: `scratch/before-capture.json`.\n\n## 3. After Enriched Embedding Text\n\n| Measure | Before | After | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Typed recall at 1 | 24 of 44 | 24 of 44 | 0 |\n| Plain tune top-1 | 13 of 45 | 18 of 45 | +5 |\n| Plain tune combined reach | 28 of 45 | 33 of 45 | +5 |\n| Plain holdout top-1 | 3 of 44 | 5 of 44 | +2 |\n| False offers | 0 of 35 | 0 of 35 | 0 |\n| `needs_mode_floor` | 1 of 35 | 1 of 35 | 0 |\n\nThe five tune rows that moved are exactly the five scored commands, each from no command to its own command at top-1:\n\n| Command | Tune | Holdout |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/doctor:install` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 |\n| `/doctor:setup` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1, unchanged |\n| `/doctor:speckit` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 |\n| `/doctor:update` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1, unchanged |\n| `/speckit:search` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1, unchanged |\n| `/create:skill-parent` | 0 of 1, unchanged | 0 of 1, unchanged |\n\nThe holdout gain is two rows and is not tune-only. No holdout prompt text was read; the per-command holdout counts come from the committed capture.\n\nEvidence: `scratch/after-capture.json`, `scratch/after-capture-rerun.json`, `scratch/after-capture-rebuilt.json`.\n\n## 4. Why the Comparison Is Isolated\n\n- The re-embed path is faithful: re-embedding the unchanged `/doctor:install` text reproduces its stored vector at cosine 1.000000.\n- Every updated row is 3,072 bytes with model `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` and a matching content hash.\n- All 14 skill vectors are byte-identical between the two database copies; exactly 5 command vectors changed, and they are the five scored commands.\n- The before capture ran twice and read 13 of 45 and 3 of 44 both times; the after capture ran three times and read 18 of 45 and 5 of 44 every time.\n\nEvidence: `scratch/metadata/reembed-report.json`, `scratch/enrich-and-embed.mjs`, `scratch/before-capture-rerun.json`.\n\n## 5. Floor Check\n\nThe three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82 still pass and still offer nothing. In the after capture each keeps `system-skilled-doctor` as its top and reads `offered: false`, `top1: false`. All three sit inside the unchanged false-offer total of 0 of 35, and `needs_mode_floor` stays at 1 of 35. The exact fused confidence was not re-read; the top skill and its skill vector are unchanged, and no command reached the top three, so the 0.82 gate is unaffected.\n\n## 6. Answer: Build\n\n**Build the five scored commands' intent signals.** The vector-only measurement already pays 5 tune rows and 2 holdout rows, with typed recall, false offers and the doctor floors unchanged. Declining would leave those 7 rows without a command for no measured floor gain.\n\n### Exact Files\n\n1. `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` — add 5 phrases to `/doctor:install`, 5 to `/doctor:setup`, 5 to `/doctor:speckit` and 4 to `/doctor:update` in their `trigger_phrases` blocks (routes at lines 626, 376, 65, 758).\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` — add 4 phrases to the `/speckit:search` `userIntent.ownedSignals` (entry at line 215).\n3. `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json` — add 4 phrases to the `/create:skill-parent` `userIntent.ownedSignals` (entry at line 48). This is a prerequisite with zero measured gain today.\n4. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` — add the `/create:skill-parent` TypeScript activation entry; rerun `derive-command-bridges.cjs` so its generated `scorerRow` flips at `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:135`.\n5. Re-embed with `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`, whose handler calls `indexSkillMetadata` then `refreshSkillEmbeddings` (`handlers/skill-graph/scan.ts:49-62`).\n\nThe exact phrases are in `scratch/metadata/enriched-embedding-text.json`. The scratch metadata copies are in `scratch/metadata/`.\n\n### Verification\n\n1. Rerun the fixture capture with `--write` to recapture the ratchet baseline; the bridge metadata changes make the old baseline stale by design.\n2. Rerun the real capture and require tune 18 of 45 or better, holdout 5 of 44 or better, false offers 0 of 35, typed recall 24 of 44.\n3. Run `route-validate.sh` and `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` for the four doctor routes.\n4. Keep the three floor rows command-free.\n\n## 7. What the Measurement Does Not Cover\n\n- **The lexical half is unmeasured.** The build also adds the same phrases to `trigger_phrases`/`ownedSignals`, which the deriver copies into the TypeScript scorer. A broad phrase such as \"list every check this project has\" could lift a near-miss or must-not-start row. The 0 of 35 false-offer gate is the control; narrow any phrase that moves it.\n- **The vector-only gain is a lower bound.** The build could gain more from lexical evidence, or less if a phrase is narrowed.\n- **Holdout is 5 of 44, not a full fix.** Two of the five scored commands gained a holdout row; three did not.\n- **`/create:skill-parent` has no scorer row.** Its measured gain is 0 until step 4 of the build lands; it is not part of the +5/+2.\n- **The exact 0.82 fused confidence was not re-read.** The top skill and its vector are unchanged, and all three rows stay silent.\n\n## 8. What This Changes in Segment Three\n\n- **Rank 10 changes from \"measure first\" to \"build\".** The measurement that changes it is the real-embedding scratch capture: tune 13 to 18 of 45, holdout 3 to 5 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, typed 24 of 44.\n- **Open question 5 is answered for command vectors**: richer command intent text moves 2 holdout rows. It is not evidence for skill-vector enrichment, so segment three rank 16 (skill intent signals) stays declined.\n- **No other rank is reopened.** The three doctor floor rows still pass, so rank 10's stated floor risk did not materialize.\n\n## 9. Convergence Report\n\n- Stop reason: `all_questions_answered`\n- Total iterations: 3\n- Questions answered: 3 of 3\n- Remaining questions: 0\n- Novelty per iteration: 0.45, 0.88, 0.35\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Note: the run stopped on question coverage, not on the 0.05 novelty threshold. Iteration 3 was synthesis with no new external measurement, and the lane instruction says to stop when a further iteration would add no new measurement.\n\n## 10. Sources\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:1484-1590`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/skill-graph/scan.ts:49-62`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:660-700`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:65,376,626,758`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json:215`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:48`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md:37,75,95,209`\n- Lineage artifacts: `iterations/iteration-001.md`, `iteration-002.md`, `iteration-003.md`; `scratch/before-capture.json`, `scratch/after-capture.json`, `scratch/metadata/enriched-embedding-text.json`, `scratch/metadata/reembed-report.json`.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/research.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/research.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/research.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: \\\"Embed text lane, segment four: what richer command embedding text buys\\\"\\ndescription: \\\"Measured answer for segment-three rank 10 and open question 5: richer intent signals and re-embedded command vectors move five no-recommendation commands on tune and two on holdout, with every floor held.\\\"\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"command embedding text research\\\"\\n  - \\\"six no-recommendation commands\\\"\\n  - \\\"segment four embed text lane\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Embed Text Lane: What Richer Command Embedding Text Buys\\n\\nLane `embed-text-4` of research segment four, measured on the built state after phases 014 and 015 at HEAD `087888ec4a`. Executor: `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` through `cli-opencode`. Three iterations, convergence threshold 0.05, stop reason `all_questions_answered`.\\n\\n## 1. What Was Measured\\n\\nSegment three rank 10 proposed giving the six no-recommendation commands evidence through command intent signals, with `/create:skill-parent` also needing a scorer row. Segment three open question 5 asked whether richer intent text in the command vectors moves holdout rows. This lane isolated the command-vector half:\\n\\n1. Took a consistent `.backup` snapshot of the live advisor database.\\n2. Added 4 to 5 intent signals per command in scratch copies of the owning metadata (the two real `command-metadata.json` files plus a command-metadata-shaped sidecar for the four doctor routes, whose tracked home is `_routes.yaml`).\\n3. Re-embedded only the five commands that own a stored vector, using the live embedder (`nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, `search_document: ` prefix).\\n4. Ran the committed capture in `--real-embedding` mode against the scratch database and compared it with the same capture against the untouched snapshot.\\n\\nThe tracked metadata, database, bridge projection and corpus were never modified. Every write is inside `research/lineages/embed-text-4/`.\\n\\n## 2. Baseline at HEAD `087888ec4a`\\n\\n| Measure | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Typed recall at 1 | 24 of 44 |\\n| Plain tune top-1 | 13 of 45 |\\n| Plain tune combined reach (own + attached) | 28 of 45 |\\n| Plain holdout top-1 | 3 of 44 |\\n| False offers | 0 of 35 |\\n| `needs_mode_floor` | 1 of 35 |\\n\\nThe three doctor-family floor rows that pass the gate at 0.82 (`mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01`, `sv-03`) all topped `system-skilled-doctor` and carried no command. Each of the five scored no-recommendation commands had one tune row and one holdout row at zero top-1 and zero top-3. `/create:skill-parent` was in the capture's `unreachable` list.\\n\\nEvidence: `scratch/before-capture.json`.\\n\\n## 3. After Enriched Embedding Text\\n\\n| Measure | Before | After | Delta |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Typed recall at 1 | 24 of 44 | 24 of 44 | 0 |\\n| Plain tune top-1 | 13 of 45 | 18 of 45 | +5 |\\n| Plain tune combined reach | 28 of 45 | 33 of 45 | +5 |\\n| Plain holdout top-1 | 3 of 44 | 5 of 44 | +2 |\\n| False offers | 0 of 35 | 0 of 35 | 0 |\\n| `needs_mode_floor` | 1 of 35 | 1 of 35 | 0 |\\n\\nThe five tune rows that moved are exactly the five scored commands, each from no command to its own command at top-1:\\n\\n| Command | Tune | Holdout |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `/doctor:install` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 |\\n| `/doctor:setup` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1, unchanged |\\n| `/doctor:speckit` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 |\\n| `/doctor:update` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1, unchanged |\\n| `/speckit:search` | 0 of 1 to 1 of 1 | 0 of 1, unchanged |\\n| `/create:skill-parent` | 0 of 1, unchanged | 0 of 1, unchanged |\\n\\nThe holdout gain is two rows and is not tune-only. No holdout prompt text was read; the per-command holdout counts come from the committed capture.\\n\\nEvidence: `scratch/after-capture.json`, `scratch/after-capture-rerun.json`, `scratch/after-capture-rebuilt.json`.\\n\\n## 4. Why the Comparison Is Isolated\\n\\n- The re-embed path is faithful: re-embedding the unchanged `/doctor:install` text reproduces its stored vector at cosine 1.000000.\\n- Every updated row is 3,072 bytes with model `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` and a matching content hash.\\n- All 14 skill vectors are byte-identical between the two database copies; exactly 5 command vectors changed, and they are the five scored commands.\\n- The before capture ran twice and read 13 of 45 and 3 of 44 both times; the after capture ran three times and read 18 of 45 and 5 of 44 every time.\\n\\nEvidence: `scratch/metadata/reembed-report.json`, `scratch/enrich-and-embed.mjs`, `scratch/before-capture-rerun.json`.\\n\\n## 5. Floor Check\\n\\nThe three doctor-family floor rows at 0.82 still pass and still offer nothing. In the after capture each keeps `system-skilled-doctor` as its top and reads `offered: false`, `top1: false`. All three sit inside the unchanged false-offer total of 0 of 35, and `needs_mode_floor` stays at 1 of 35. The exact fused confidence was not re-read; the top skill and its skill vector are unchanged, and no command reached the top three, so the 0.82 gate is unaffected.\\n\\n## 6. Answer: Build\\n\\n**Build the five scored commands' intent signals.** The vector-only measurement already pays 5 tune rows and 2 holdout rows, with typed recall, false offers and the doctor floors unchanged. Declining would leave those 7 rows without a command for no measured floor gain.\\n\\n### Exact Files\\n\\n1. `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` — add 5 phrases to `/doctor:install`, 5 to `/doctor:setup`, 5 to `/doctor:speckit` and 4 to `/doctor:update` in their `trigger_phrases` blocks (routes at lines 626, 376, 65, 758).\\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` — add 4 phrases to the `/speckit:search` `userIntent.ownedSignals` (entry at line 215).\\n3. `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json` — add 4 phrases to the `/create:skill-parent` `userIntent.ownedSignals` (entry at line 48). This is a prerequisite with zero measured gain today.\\n4. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` — add the `/create:skill-parent` TypeScript activation entry; rerun `derive-command-bridges.cjs` so its generated `scorerRow` flips at `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:135`.\\n5. Re-embed with `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`, whose handler calls `indexSkillMetadata` then `refreshSkillEmbeddings` (`handlers/skill-graph/scan.ts:49-62`).\\n\\nThe exact phrases are in `scratch/metadata/enriched-embedding-text.json`. The scratch metadata copies are in `scratch/metadata/`.\\n\\n### Verification\\n\\n1. Rerun the fixture capture with `--write` to recapture the ratchet baseline; the bridge metadata changes make the old baseline stale by design.\\n2. Rerun the real capture and require tune 18 of 45 or better, holdout 5 of 44 or better, false offers 0 of 35, typed recall 24 of 44.\\n3. Run `route-validate.sh` and `doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` for the four doctor routes.\\n4. Keep the three floor rows command-free.\\n\\n## 7. What the Measurement Does Not Cover\\n\\n- **The lexical half is unmeasured.** The build also adds the same phrases to `trigger_phrases`/`ownedSignals`, which the deriver copies into the TypeScript scorer. A broad phrase such as \\\"list every check this project has\\\" could lift a near-miss or must-not-start row. The 0 of 35 false-offer gate is the control; narrow any phrase that moves it.\\n- **The vector-only gain is a lower bound.** The build could gain more from lexical evidence, or less if a phrase is narrowed.\\n- **Holdout is 5 of 44, not a full fix.** Two of the five scored commands gained a holdout row; three did not.\\n- **`/create:skill-parent` has no scorer row.** Its measured gain is 0 until step 4 of the build lands; it is not part of the +5/+2.\\n- **The exact 0.82 fused confidence was not re-read.** The top skill and its vector are unchanged, and all three rows stay silent.\\n\\n## 8. What This Changes in Segment Three\\n\\n- **Rank 10 changes from \\\"measure first\\\" to \\\"build\\\".** The measurement that changes it is the real-embedding scratch capture: tune 13 to 18 of 45, holdout 3 to 5 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, typed 24 of 44.\\n- **Open question 5 is answered for command vectors**: richer command intent text moves 2 holdout rows. It is not evidence for skill-vector enrichment, so segment three rank 16 (skill intent signals) stays declined.\\n- **No other rank is reopened.** The three doctor floor rows still pass, so rank 10's stated floor risk did not materialize.\\n\\n## 9. Convergence Report\\n\\n- Stop reason: `all_questions_answered`\\n- Total iterations: 3\\n- Questions answered: 3 of 3\\n- Remaining questions: 0\\n- Novelty per iteration: 0.45, 0.88, 0.35\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Note: the run stopped on question coverage, not on the 0.05 novelty threshold. Iteration 3 was synthesis with no new external measurement, and the lane instruction says to stop when a further iteration would add no new measurement.\\n\\n## 10. Sources\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts:1484-1590`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/skill-graph/scan.ts:49-62`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:660-700`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:65,376,626,758`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json:215`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:48`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md:37,75,95,209`\\n- Lineage artifacts: `iterations/iteration-001.md`, `iteration-002.md`, `iteration-003.md`; `scratch/before-capture.json`, `scratch/after-capture.json`, `scratch/metadata/enriched-embedding-text.json`, `scratch/metadata/reembed-report.json`.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/embed-text-4/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571278571,"end":1794571300656}}}}
